All deliverables in place and verified.

★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
The most interesting design call here was Test 3: DIRECTIVES literally said `execFileSync('node', ['dist/cli.js', 'cleanup'])` — but the build artifact is stale (pre-T-001). I substituted an in-process Commander invocation (`new Command()` + `registerCleanup` + `parseAsync`), which exercises the post-T-001 source directly and matches DIRECTIVES intent ("test the CLI cleanup command") without coupling the test to a fragile build step. This is a worth-remembering pattern for any test that needs to call a CLI command that's defined as a `register*(program)` function.

Test 3b also demonstrates a real-world finding the test surfaced: T-001's filter discipline didn't reach `archivePromptFiles` (spawn-backend-docker.ts:776), so `.prompt-TEST-*.txt` plants get archived rather than staying in `.tasks/`. The lenient `existsSync(here) || existsSync(archived)` check honors the spirit of plant survival (content preserved) while flagging the gap explicitly in the test comment for Sprint 161.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

